  "description": "The Budgets area on one small imager in a 550 km Sun-synchronous orbit: 12 items, four system modes, the power, mass, pointing and propellant budgets. Each number of the budgets is an example, and its source says so.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- Budgets > Equipment: the items with mass and maturity, their power modes, the system modes, the power settings.\n- Budgets > Power: each mode's load, margins and source power. The duty cycles add up to 1, so the last row is the average: 54.2 W of load, 77.1 W at the source with margins.\n- Budgets > Mass: 110.3 kg basic and 22.9 kg of AIAA S-120 growth; with 6 kg of propellant, 139.2 kg against the 150 kg limit.\n- Budgets > Pointing: three requirements met; the line of sight at 22.1 of 60 arcsec (0.95).\n- Budgets > Propellant, Compute budget: 83.0 m/s and 5.23 kg for five years, in an 8 kg tank (about a minute).\n\nTry changing:\n- A mode's duty cycle: when they no longer add up to 1, the average row goes and Problems says why.\n- Clear the camera's imaging power (it becomes TBD): the Power badge says Unknown values.\n- Power settings: the system margin or a bus's efficiency.\n\nNote:\n- The 3D model holds every item (Mass in model): the run flies the same 110.3 kg.",
  "schema_version": 8
}
